---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FAQBlock from '../components/FAQBlock.astro';
import CTABlock from '../components/CTABlock.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import GradientBackdrop from '../components/GradientBackdrop.astro';

const aboutSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Organization',
  'name': site.name,
  'url': site.url,
  'knowsAbout': ['Dental Website Design', 'SEO', 'Web Development', 'AI-Assisted Development'],
};

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Why dental websites specifically?',
    answer: 'Dentists are some of the most skilled professionals we know, and some of the most underserved when it comes to their online presence. They don\'t have time to learn web development, and they shouldn\'t have to. The dental marketing industry has been overcharging for underwhelming work for years. Modern tools make it possible to deliver dramatically better results at a fraction of the cost. Dentists were the obvious place to start.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Why no traditional agency overhead?',
    answer: 'Modern AI tools compress what used to take separate designers, developers, and copywriters into a focused build. The savings go to you. No account managers. No layers between you and the work — you talk to whoever is actually building your site, not a sales rep or a PM relaying messages.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What happens if you get hit by a bus?',
    answer: 'Your website keeps working. It\'s hosted on Cloudflare (which isn\'t going anywhere), the code is on GitHub, and any developer in the world can pick it up. That\'s the whole ownership model — you\'re never locked into a single vendor.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you use AI? Is that a problem?',
    answer: 'Yes, and no. The page you\'re reading right now was built with the help of AI — doesn\'t it look good? Every agency in 2026 is using AI. Most just won\'t admit it because they\'re still charging 2019 prices. We\'re upfront about it because it\'s why the service costs $2,000 instead of $15,000. The AI does the heavy lifting; we do the quality control, customization, and engineering that AI can\'t handle on its own yet.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Groundwork Dental — Why This Exists"
  description="Dentists deserve better websites. Professional, fast, search-optimized — with full ownership and no monthly fees. Here's why we built this."
  schema={aboutSchema}
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative isolate bg-surface-2">
    <GradientBackdrop intensity={0.68} />
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 md:py-16">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h1 class="section-heading mb-6">You're a Dentist, Not a Web Developer.</h1>
        <p class="font-serif text-xl text-mid-gray leading-relaxed">
          You're great at dentistry. You shouldn't have to be great at websites too.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Story -->
  <section class="py-10">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="prose-card prose-article text-lg">
        <h2>Where This Started</h2>
        <p>
          Groundwork was born out of watching several dentist family members struggle to build a website themselves or pay way too much for one that never changed.
        </p>
        <p>
          The need isn't complicated. A clear website and Google Business Profile that patients can actually find. Most practices don't need a complex website or a marketing department. They're established businesses that just need to show up where patients are looking — without wasting their time or overpaying for it.
        </p>

        <h2>Why This Costs $2,000 Instead of $15,000</h2>
        <p>
          You or your tech-savvy niece could technically build a website with AI tools today. Seriously — if you've used ChatGPT, you're halfway there. The other half is where things start breaking: your SSL certificate expires, your sitemap isn't submitting, your schema markup is invalid, your structured data doesn't match what Google expects, and your contact form is emailing submissions into the void.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use AI. We're upfront about it. The page you're reading right now was built with the help of AI — looks clean, right? Every agency in 2026 is using AI. If they aren't, that's a problem. It builds faster, makes fewer mistakes, but it's only as good as the person using it. We say the quiet part out loud: AI is why this costs $2,000 instead of $15,000. But there's still a lot that goes on in the background — writing, hosting, coding, configuration — that ChatGPT can't quite do on its own yet. We could teach you all of that, but it would cost more than $2,000 and take longer than 7 days. Which is what we're offering.
        </p>

        <h2>What We Actually Promise</h2>
        <p>
          We're not here to game Google's algorithm. Not to chase it, trick it, or exploit techniques that work until the next update kills them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every dental marketing agency promises guaranteed rankings and more patients. Press them on how, and the answer is almost always paid ads — clicks rented by the month that disappear the day you stop paying. That's not an SEO foundation. That's a lever someone else holds.
        </p>
        <p>
          Here's what we actually do: Google and AI search engines (ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews) send agents to evaluate your site constantly. Those agents are asking a specific set of questions. Does this practice load in under a second on mobile? Is the Google Business Profile verified, accurate, and complete? Is the structured data valid? Does this look like an established, trustworthy dental practice serving patients in this area? We build sites that answer every one of those questions correctly — because Google publishes exactly what it's looking for, and the honest move is just to build that.
        </p>
        <p>
          That's the whole promise. Not guaranteed rankings. Not more patients in your chair next month. A site that checks every box Google runs — permanently, at no ongoing cost, owned entirely by you.
        </p>
        <p>
          The bar is low. We clear it by a lot.
        </p>
        <p>
          Real growth beyond that requires regular content creation — more articles, more engagement, maybe even TikToks. Let's crawl before we walk. And when we're done here, everything is yours. Hire someone else, or never talk to us again. Your website keeps working. We walk away clean.
        </p>

        <h2>Who This Is NOT For</h2>
        <p>
          If you want a $30,000 fully custom marketing website with a full design team — that exists, and that's fine. This isn't that.
        </p>
        <p>
          We don't run paid campaigns. If you eventually want Google Ads or Meta, hire someone good, and they'll thank you for having a solid site to send traffic to. But a lot of practices with a good foundation never feel the need to run ads at all. The organic baseline goes further than most people expect.
        </p>
        <p>
          We build the website foundation. We don't run a marketing department. But we'll happily tell you what to look for and what to avoid so you don't get burned. That advice is free.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="py-10 relative isolate bg-surface-2">
    <GradientBackdrop intensity={0.68} />
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <FAQBlock faqs={faqs} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="py-10">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <CTABlock
        heading="Want to See What We Build?"
        subheading="Check out a live example of a dental website we've built. Click around. Test the speed. Then decide if you want one."
        primaryCTA="See an Example"
        primaryHref="/example"
        secondaryCTA="View pricing"
        secondaryHref="/pricing"
        variant="dark"
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
